  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Server Setup**\n\nOkay, I\'m now delving into the specific server setup requirements. I see that for the development environment with an iFrame, port 3000 is non-negotiable. For a full-stack approach, I\'m thinking of an Express server running through `server.ts` alongside `vite`. I am examining how these configurations will handle API routes and data retrieval.\n\n\n**Refining Server Scripts**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the `package.json` scripts. I\'ve updated the scripts, considering both development and deployment scenarios. For development, I\'ll use `\"dev\": \"tsx server.ts\"`. For deployment, I can set up `\"start\": \"node server.js\"` after a build step, or directly use `\"start\": \"tsx server.ts\"`. I am planning to address server startup and potential build commands next.\n\n\n**Evaluating Model Choice**\n\nI am now assessing the best Large Language Model (LLM) options. I plan to start with `gemini-2.5-flash` per the blueprint. If it\'s unavailable, I will automatically fallback to `gemini-3.8-flash`, or vice versa depending on availability and performance. The system instruction is setting the stage for me.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Security Measures**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on security protocols. I\'m making sure all secrets, tokens, and bearer headers are sourced from environment variables, never hardcoded. I\'m planning to implement comprehensive try-catch wrappers around network calls for structured error returns to the agent, marking errors clearly as such. Crucially, I\'m validating input schema to guard against injection.\n\n\n\n**Generating Configuration Files**\n\nI am now focusing on generating essential configuration files. I\'m building `mcp_config.json`, `README.md`, and `.env.example` templates, essential for streamlined setup. Furthermore, I\'m working to make sure there\'s a robust client fallback in place; if the API key is missing or there\'s a network failure, the user should instantly get an MCP server ready for cURL/OpenAPI, complete with all necessary components. With a valid key, I\'ll leverage Gemini AI for JSON output.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_669450"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Update dev and start scripts in package.json for full-stack Express + Vite\",\"EndLine\":13,\"Instruction\":\"Update dev and start scripts\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"tsx server.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"vite build\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"tsx server.ts\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"rm -rf dist server.js\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit\\\"\\n  },\",\"StartLine\":6,\"TargetContent\":\"  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\\\",\\n    \\\"build\\\": \\\"vite build\\\",\\n    \\\"preview\\\": \\\"vite preview\\\",\\n    \\\"clean\\\": \\\"rm -rf dist server.js\\\",\\n    \\\"lint\\\": \\\"tsc --noEmit\\\"\\n  },\",\"TargetFile\":\"/package.json\",\"toolAction\":\"Editing package.json scripts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Update scripts in package.json\"}"
