  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Requirements**\n\nI\'ve successfully compiled the project with TypeScript, ensuring zero errors with `tsc --noEmit`. Now, the focus shifts to meticulous front-end design, and I\'m reviewing the user\'s requirements: the project\'s language is confirmed to be English. I\'m also incorporating the Google AI Studio Blueprint `c`.\n\n\n**Generating Server-Side Code**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress! My thoughts now center on generating the server-side code: I\'ve created an Edge Worker/Express proxy (`/api/generate`) that successfully takes user input, calls the Gemini API, and returns structured JSON. I\'m focusing on providing users with one-click copy buttons for key files (`index.ts`, `mcp_config.json`, and `package.json`), as well as a \'Download as ZIP\' option for a complete, runnable package.\n\n\n**Designing Exceptional Features**\n\nI am now focused on defining outstanding features. I\'m imagining a multi-file IDE with tabs, line numbers, and syntax highlighting. I\'m also considering a language switch between TypeScript and Python. The goal is to provide a Tool Inspector with interactive playgrounds, including visual cards for server tools, extracted input schemas, and live mock request runners. A badge bar will also be added to show environment variables, and guide to set up Claude Desktop.\n\n\n**Defining Enhanced Features**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining enhanced features. My focus includes a \"Cursor & Antigravity\" quick toggle, complete with step-by-step instructions. I\'m also adding a System Instruction blueprint viewer with a copy button for seamless AI Studio replication, and incorporating generation history and presets in `localStorage`. There will be a status indicator for the Gemini backend connection, too. I\'m investigating the styling in `src/index.css`, ensuring it harmonizes with modern fonts and scrollbars, aiming for a sleek, developer-focused aesthetic. Finally, I\'m working on defining types, constants and components.\n\n\n**Constructing Interface Components**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in constructing the interface components. I\'m focusing on the top bar, complete with logo, brand identity, and essential links. I\'m building `InputPanel.tsx` with preset pills, a language toggle (TypeScript vs. Python), and a \"Generate MCP Server\" button with loading states. For `CodeViewer.tsx`, I am working on a multi-file tab navigation with line numbers, copy buttons, and download options, to be able to be downloaded one-by-one or all at once, as a ZIP. I\'m also planning the `ToolPlayground.tsx` with a visual tool list and interactive schema visualizer.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_496707"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"export type McpLanguage = \'typescript\' | \'python\';\\n\\nexport interface GeneratedFile {\\n  path: string;\\n  content: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface McpGenerationSummary {\\n  toolsGenerated: string[];\\n  requiredEnvVars: string[];\\n  description?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface McpServerResponse {\\n  serverName: string;\\n  language: McpLanguage;\\n  files: GeneratedFile[];\\n  summary: McpGenerationSummary;\\n  generatedBy?: string;\\n  notice?: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface PresetSnippet {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  category: \'cURL\' | \'OpenAPI\' | \'Swagger\';\\n  language: McpLanguage;\\n  serverName: string;\\n  snippet: string;\\n  description: string;\\n}\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create TypeScript type definitions for MCP server generator\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/mcp.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Writing types\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create src/types/mcp.ts\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
    thinking_duration {
