  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Performance Bottlenecks**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on the root cause of those lengthy initial `curl` times. It looks like the model spends a significant chunk of time \342\200\223 roughly 18-20 seconds \342\200\223 generating those comprehensive configuration files right from the outset. This seems like a promising avenue for optimization.\n\n\n**Enhancing User Experience**\n\nI\'m focusing on making the generation process feel less like a black box. I\'ve decided to add dynamic progress messages to the frontend. The \"Generate\" button, currently in `InputPanel.tsx`, will display real-time updates: \"Analyzing API...\", \"Synthesizing Zod schemas...\", etc., improving the user\'s perception of the delay. I\'m also planning to add preset descriptions and specific labeling of test cases.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_871302"
      name: "replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"AllowMultiple\":false,\"Description\":\"Add dynamic progress steps and enhance presets in InputPanel.tsx\",\"EndLine\":60,\"Instruction\":\"Add dynamic progress steps and enhanced descriptions\",\"ReplacementContent\":\"  const [copied, setCopied] = React.useState(false);\\n  const [generationStep, setGenerationStep] = React.useState(0);\\n\\n  const GENERATION_STEPS = [\\n    \'Analyzing API specification & paths...\',\\n    \'Extracting headers into environment variables...\',\\n    \'Synthesizing deterministic TypeSafe Zod schemas...\',\\n    \'Wiring up @modelcontextprotocol/sdk handlers...\',\\n    \'Packaging project files and client configuration...\',\\n  ];\\n\\n  React.useEffect(() => {\\n    let interval: any;\\n    if (isGenerating) {\\n      setGenerationStep(0);\\n      interval = setInterval(() => {\\n        setGenerationStep((prev) => (prev + 1) % GENERATION_STEPS.length);\\n      }, 2500);\\n    } else {\\n      setGenerationStep(0);\\n    }\\n    return () => clearInterval(interval);\\n  }, [isGenerating]);\\n\\n  const handleCopyInput = () => {\",\"StartLine\":34,\"TargetContent\":\"  const [copied, setCopied] = React.useState(false);\\n\\n  const handleCopyInput = () => {\",\"TargetFile\":\"/src/components/InputPanel.tsx\",\"toolAction\":\"Updating InputPanel.tsx\",\"toolSummary\":\"Add dynamic generation progress in InputPanel\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "replace_file_content"
    }
    thinking_duration {
